@* M-D1 requirement 4 (TRUNCATION AUDIT, owner priority statement 2026-08-21:
   truncating hover-menu output "we need that to improve user experience" --
   ranked ABOVE new features): a place's own EVENTS section
   (PlaceEventsSection, Explore/PopoverSectionProviders.cs) rendered every
   located-at event with NO cap at all -- a real, live-verified gap (a
   central place like Jerusalem carries 236 events across the whole atlas'
   own timeline; the popover would have rendered all 236 rows). This is now
   the ONE place that list renders, following VerseTextSectionProvider's own
   established precedent ("hand the actual rendering to a real component...
   unlike a hand-built RenderFragment, this owns real interactive STATE a
   closure has no clean way to hold") -- PlaceEventsSection itself is a
   static, provider-instance-shared RenderFragment builder and cannot safely
   own a per-popover "expanded" bool; this component can.

   Same down-arrow reveal AFFORDANCE/CSS class (.popover-passage-reveal) and
   glyphs (▾/▲) PassageList.razor's own Cap mechanism already established --
   "reuse the shared bits" even where the CONTENT shape (event summary rows,
   not passage text blocks) does not fit PassageList itself. *@
@using BibleAtlas.Client.Explore

@{
    var shown = _showAll ? Events : Events.Take(Cap);
}
@foreach (var e in shown)
{
    var ev = e; // local copy -- captured per-row by the onclick closure below
    <button type="button" class="popover-event-row popover-event-row-button explorable" data-testid="@($"place-event-{ev.Id}")"
            @onclick="() => OnExplore.InvokeAsync(new TimeAndPlaceNode(PlaceName, ev.When, ev.Label, ev.VerseGroups))">
        <span class="popover-event-label">@ev.Label</span>
        <span class="popover-event-years">@YearText.FormatRange(ev.When.FromYear, ev.When.ToYear)</span>
    </button>
}

@if (Events.Count > Cap)
{
    @if (!_showAll)
    {
        <button type="button" class="popover-passage-reveal" data-testid="place-events-more" aria-label="@($"Show {Events.Count - Cap} more events")"
                @onclick="() => _showAll = true">&#9662;</button>
    }
    else
    {
        <button type="button" class="popover-passage-reveal" data-testid="place-events-collapse" aria-label="Show fewer events"
                @onclick="() => _showAll = false">&#9652;</button>
    }
}

@code {
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public string PlaceName { get; set; } = default!;
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public List<SceneEvent> Events { get; set; } = new();
    [Parameter] public int Cap { get; set; } = 10;
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public EventCallback<IExplorable> OnExplore { get; set; }

    private bool _showAll;
}
